.TH IO_RESET 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
iob_reset \- Reset the I/O batch buffer

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/iob_internal.h>

.IB void
.IB iob_reset(
.IB io_batch* b
.IB );

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBiob_reset\fR function resets the I/O batch buffer. This function is used to clear the contents of the I/O batch buffer and free any associated resources.

The function takes the following parameter:

.IB b
Pointer to the I/O batch buffer.

The function does not return any value.

The function is part of the \fBiob\fR library, which provides a framework for managing I/O operations in batch mode.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBiob_reset\fR function to reset the I/O batch buffer:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/iob.h>

int main() {
  io_batch* batch = iob_new(100); // Hint for 100 entries
  if (!batch) {
    perror("iob_new");
    return 1;
  }

  // Add data to the batch buffer
  iob_adds(batch, "Hello, World!");
  iob_adds(batch, "This is a test.");

  // Reset the I/O batch buffer
  iob_reset(batch);

  // Check if the batch buffer is empty
  if (iob_bytesleft(batch) == 0) {
    printf("I/O batch buffer is empty after reset\n");
  }

  // Free the I/O batch buffer
  iob_free(batch);

  return 0;
}
.nef